WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.157
At school on Monday morning, Katie was mad, but she was also worried.

2
00:00:08.158 --> 00:00:14.277
If she didn’t make up with Luke and Carlos, her square-dance plans were finished.

3
00:00:14.278 --> 00:00:17.590
She handed a note to Joy.

4
00:00:17.591 --> 00:00:21.215
"Please pass this to Carlos," she said.

5
00:00:21.216 --> 00:00:23.287
She gave a note to Olivia.

6
00:00:23.288 --> 00:00:26.103
"Please pass this to Luke."

7
00:00:26.104 --> 00:00:28.275
The notes said the same thing:

8
00:00:28.276 --> 00:00:33.100
Come to dance practice tonight!

9
00:00:33.101 --> 00:00:38.565
N-O spells NO , wrote

10
00:00:38.566 --> 00:00:43.899
Carlos. NO WAY ,

11
00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:49.627
wrote Luke. "It’s time for Laura’s report on eyes," said

12
00:00:49.628 --> 00:00:54.625
Ms. Barrow. Laura carried a small pink suitcase to the front of

13
00:00:54.626 --> 00:00:59.678
the room. "Everyone, I’m worried about your eyes!" she

14
00:00:59.679 --> 00:01:01.595
said. "You must protect

15
00:01:01.596 --> 00:01:05.163
them!" Her eyes got big behind her

16
00:01:05.164 --> 00:01:09.423
glasses. "Watch out for sharp things—like

17
00:01:09.424 --> 00:01:14.269
scissors!" Joy remembered when Katie ran down the steps with

18
00:01:14.270 --> 00:01:18.722
scissors. She kicked Katie’s desk to make sure she was

19
00:01:18.723 --> 00:01:24.299
listening. Laura continued. "Watch out for flying things—like

20
00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:28.705
darts. And exploding things—like

21
00:01:28.706 --> 00:01:32.429
firecrackers. And things that splash—like paint

22
00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:35.646
remover!" Laura reached inside her

23
00:01:35.647 --> 00:01:39.411
suitcase. "These are safety glasses," she

24
00:01:39.412 --> 00:01:42.257
said. "They fit over regular

25
00:01:42.258 --> 00:01:47.408
glasses. Wear them when you do science experiments or use

26
00:01:47.409 --> 00:01:50.472
tools." Laura pulled out more

27
00:01:50.473 --> 00:01:56.607
glasses. "These are very cool sports glasses that I wear when I play

28
00:01:56.608 --> 00:02:01.953
softball. And these sunglasses protect my eyes from harmful

29
00:02:01.954 --> 00:02:09.083
sunrays. "If you have trouble reading your books or seeing what Ms. Barrow writes on the board, tell your

30
00:02:09.084 --> 00:02:11.264
parents. Maybe you need

31
00:02:11.265 --> 00:02:13.848
glasses. I wear glasses all the

32
00:02:13.849 --> 00:02:17.534
time. If I take them off, I look weird!

33
00:02:17.535 --> 00:02:19.840
See? I don’t even look like

34
00:02:19.841 --> 00:02:21.996
me!" Laura closed her

35
00:02:21.997 --> 00:02:26.359
suitcase. "Thank you," she said and returned to her

36
00:02:26.360 --> 00:02:29.973
desk. "That was great!" Joy told

37
00:02:29.974 --> 00:02:32.343
her. Next was Joy’s

38
00:02:32.344 --> 00:02:36.368
presentation. "I’m going to talk about how to build

39
00:02:36.369 --> 00:02:41.424
friendships. First, I want you all to be friendly listeners during my

40
00:02:41.425 --> 00:02:45.781
report. Please turn your bodies toward me and look into my eyes."

41
00:02:45.782 --> 00:02:48.705
Joy looked around the room.

42
00:02:48.706 --> 00:02:53.631
"Good. Now, while I’m talking, don’t let your mind wander off.

43
00:02:53.632 --> 00:02:56.698
Pay attention!" She smiled.

44
00:02:56.699 --> 00:03:00.293
"Is everybody ready to be a friendly listener?"

45
00:03:00.294 --> 00:03:02.934
Everyone nodded at Joy.

46
00:03:02.935 --> 00:03:08.768
"If you see someone who looks like a nice person, say something friendly.

47
00:03:08.769 --> 00:03:12.093
That’s how to start a new friendship.

48
00:03:12.094 --> 00:03:16.096
You could offer to help carry groceries or books.

49
00:03:16.097 --> 00:03:17.975
The opposite works too!

50
00:03:17.976 --> 00:03:20.464
Ask someone to help you

51
00:03:20.465 --> 00:03:26.317
!" Katie nodded. She remembered how Olivia had asked for help at the

52
00:03:26.318 --> 00:03:30.149
library. She turned and smiled at her new

53
00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:36.314
friend. "You can also say someone has a nice haircut or cute sneakers," said

54
00:03:36.315 --> 00:03:42.346
Joy. "On the first day of school, Laura told Olivia that her kukui nut necklace was

55
00:03:42.347 --> 00:03:44.587
cool. That was a friendly thing to

56
00:03:44.588 --> 00:03:49.879
say." Joy took a breath, smiled at Laura, and

57
00:03:49.880 --> 00:03:54.169
continued. "Here are some other ways to be a good friend," she

58
00:03:54.170 --> 00:03:57.743
said. "Be kind. Don’t make fun of your

59
00:03:57.744 --> 00:04:01.566
friends." "Does that mean don’t tease?" asked

60
00:04:01.567 --> 00:04:04.012
Katie. She looked at

61
00:04:04.013 --> 00:04:06.799
Luke. "Make sure your friends can count on

62
00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:10.271
you. Don’t back out on promises or

63
00:04:10.272 --> 00:04:13.704
plans." Luke and Carlos looked at

64
00:04:13.705 --> 00:04:19.326
Katie. "Don’t be bossy," said

65
00:04:19.327 --> 00:04:23.245
Joy. "Why is everyone looking at me?" cried Katie.

66
00:04:23.246 --> 00:04:27.090
"Let’s be good listeners," said Ms. Barrow.

67
00:04:27.091 --> 00:04:30.451
"That means no interrupting."

68
00:04:30.452 --> 00:04:34.594
"Now this is important," Joy went on.

69
00:04:34.595 --> 00:04:39.736
"If you fight with your friends, make up as soon as you can.

70
00:04:39.737 --> 00:04:43.167
Say, ‘I’m sorry. I shouldn’t have said that.’

71
00:04:43.168 --> 00:04:46.383
Or say, ‘I made a mistake.’"

72
00:04:46.384 --> 00:04:49.794
Joy reached into a paper bag.

73
00:04:49.795 --> 00:04:53.665
"This is my friendship meter," she said.

74
00:04:53.666 --> 00:04:59.194
"Right now some friends in this room are making the friendship meter unhappy."

75
00:04:59.195 --> 00:05:04.312
Joy looked at Luke, then Carlos, then Katie.

76
00:05:04.313 --> 00:05:07.692
"The friends have had a fight," she said.

77
00:05:07.693 --> 00:05:13.102
"But I think it’s time to make up!"

